The desk merged every date report into #4471. The reports describe **two failures**, so the
ticket's “one issue, one fix” summary cannot cover them both. The table below counts distinct
report IDs, grouped by the tenant's date locale, booking form, and report channel. It reads the
current export when the page renders, so a newer export can change the counts.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## 1. Shared parser reads month first

The shared parser treats a date as `MM/DD/YYYY`. These tenants write the day before the month.
When both numbers are at most 12, a date can land in another month instead of failing visibly.
This affects app and email reports, and form reports from tenants whose form shows the day-first
`DD/MM/YYYY` hint. The parser group is the cause that belongs to #4471.

**Outcome: fixed.** The desk's 5 October engineering update records
`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. Verify ambiguous and unambiguous dates in the affected
locales when checking the fix.

[Track the parser failure](https://github.com/renzop/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).

## 2. Booking form hint contradicts tenant date order

The `booking-v3` form shows `MM/DD/YYYY` to people at day-first tenants. A person can follow that
hint, but the form then reads the entered date in the tenant's day-first order. This is a form
hint failure, distinct from the shared parser. It occurs on form reports for the affected
`booking-v3` tenants and needs its own ticket.

**Outcome: won't fix.** The desk says `booking-v3` was retired. Keep this cause separate in the
incident record: the parser fix did not make the old form hint truthful. If this form returns,
make its displayed hint match the date order it accepts and test entry in each tenant locale.

[Track the form hint failure](https://github.com/renzop/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

<Callout kind="warn">
Intake's `meta.intakeTag` comes from the reporter's browser locale. Do not use it, the subject
line, or the apparent size of a date shift to assign a cause. Use tenant locale, booking form,
and channel. The desk's one-day-move notes remain counted under their assigned cause.
</Callout>

The desk [closed #4471 on 5 October](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows) after that
engineering update. The two linked tickets record different outcomes for the two causes.

